    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304-a3">

                <pb facs="0692" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg644"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hiogo,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 5, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Present, the representatives of France, Great Britain, Italy, the Netherlands,
                    Prussia, and the United States.</p>
                <p>The undersigned, having come to the conclusion, after mature deliberation, that
                    it is of great importance to hold the foreign settlement at this place, resolve
                    to invite the respective commanding officers to take into their hands the entire
                    military management of this measure, and to inform them what part of the town or
                    settlement they can hold with the force at their disposal.</p>
                <pb facs="0693" n="645" xml:id="pg645"/>
                <p>The undersigned, however, would wish to see that part of Kobé in actual
                    occupation of foreigners protected, if this be possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LEON ROCHES.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HARRY S. PARKES.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CTE. DE LA TOUR.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. B. VAN VALKENBURGH.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. VON BRANDT.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <signed>D. DE GRAEF VAN POLSBROEK.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
